The header wrapper itself is the expensive composition, so I’m removing it. It is unnecessary now that the final target is relational: fixed semantics can execute allocation, division, and the loop test; on a positive count it reaches the already-proven body cut directly, and on zero it exits directly. The parity-tail claim then consumes the loop relation.
